    {
      "id": "7da36886-ee43-4216-a301-7bea286f7e6e",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        464,
        -3216
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 1312,
        "content": "## AI Batch Deviation Root-Cause Investigator\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow receives a submitted batch deviation, prepares the investigation context, and uses an AI agent to investigate likely root causes using equipment, operator, environmental, and historical CAPA data. It logs the AI-generated root-cause analysis to Postgres, then branches based on confidence: low-confidence cases are routed for manual investigation, while sufficient-confidence cases go through QA review. If QA approves, the workflow updates the QMS deviation record, optionally creates a draft CAPA, and posts a final investigation summary to Slack.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the webhook URL and ensure the submitting system sends deviationId, batchId, product, and deviationDescription or compatible fields for the Set - Config node.\n- Add credentials for OpenAI Chat Model and configure the AI Agent prompt, model, and memory settings.\n- Configure the AI tool connections for equipment events, operator actions, environmental data, and historical CAPA vector search, including any required API keys or internal network access.\n- Set up Postgres credentials and confirm the RCA investigation logging table/schema matches the insert or update performed by the Postgres node.\n- Configure Slack credentials, target channels, and message templates for QA review, manual investigation notices, rejection notices, and final summaries.\n- Configure QMS API credentials and endpoints for updating deviation records and creating optional CAPA draft records.\n- Verify the Wait node resume behavior and QA approval payload format so the IF - QA Approved condition can evaluate decisions correctly.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the AI investigation prompt, confidence threshold, QA approval logic, CAPA recommendation criteria, Slack channels, and QMS endpoint mappings to match the organization’s deviation and CAPA process."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "9df30033-df1c-4cfa-8a01-e2ea46454f38",
